{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2997","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2997","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2997\",\"parent_revision\":\"a3f154b13a470b2ab180cde237792c158cb6bbf03fb9da4c464016f0cb3e37da\",\"root_revision\":\"a3f154b13a470b2ab180cde237792c158cb6bbf03fb9da4c464016f0cb3e37da\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe active branch ruleset on `main` (id 20773573, verify current state via `gh api repos/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/rulesets/20773573`) has its `required_status_checks` rule's `strict_required_status_checks_policy` parameter set to `false`. This is the literal, mechanical cause of the exact bug class this repo's session on 2026-08-18 spent ~2 hours diagnosing on PR #2983: `actions/checkout@v6` on a `pull_request` trigger tests the *merge* of a PR branch into `main`, but a PR's CI run is only re-triggered on push to that PR's own branch \u2014 if `main` moves forward after the PR's last push (landing a conflicting or overlapping fix), the PR's displayed CI status can stay green while the actual merge result would fail, and nothing in this repo's current CI configuration re-checks that before allowing merge. `strict_required_status_checks_policy: true` is GitHub's literal name for \\\"require branches to be up to date with the base branch before merging\\\" \u2014 flipping it directly closes this gap.\\n\\nThis is distinct from and complementary to #2989 (which covers WHICH checks are required \u2014 currently only 3 of ~12 real jobs) and #2990 (a *symptom* of a bypass-actor misconfiguration on the same ruleset, made while addressing this problem class). This item is scoped specifically to the `strict_required_status_checks_policy` flag.\\n\\n**Caveat that must be checked before flipping this flag** (do not skip during implementation): `.github/workflows/auto-rebase.yml` exists and rebases a PR branch onto `main` (triggered via `/rebase` comment or an `autorebase` label, using `peter-evans/rebase@v3`). If that workflow pushes using the default `secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN` rather than a PAT, the push does not re-trigger this repo's CI workflows (a documented GitHub Actions limitation, and this repo's own `code-quality.yml` has a comment noting exactly this). If `strict_required_status_checks_policy` is turned on before that token is swapped to a PAT, every auto-rebased PR becomes permanently stuck: rebased-but-never-re-checked, so it can never satisfy \\\"up to date with base\\\" + \\\"checks passed\\\" simultaneously. Verify `auto-rebase.yml`'s push credential and switch it to a PAT (or equivalent) FIRST, then flip the ruleset flag, then verify with one real PR that an auto-rebase actually re-triggers CI before considering this closed.\\n\\nMerge-cadence context for whoever implements this (checked 2026-08-18): mean 4.2 merges/day over the last 300 PRs, max 26 in one day, but that volume was a sequential merge chain (not many PRs open and racing concurrently \u2014 usually 1-3 open at once) and median CI wall time is ~3.3 minutes, so strict-mode's rebase-and-rerun cost is small in practice. A GitHub merge queue is NOT recommended for this repo's actual usage pattern \u2014 that's higher ceremony than this problem needs.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `auto-rebase.yml` push credential verified/upgraded to a PAT (or equivalent) so pushes it makes re-trigger CI workflows\\n- [ ] `strict_required_status_checks_policy` set to `true` on ruleset id 20773573\\n- [ ] Verified with one real PR that an auto-rebase actually re-triggers CI before considering this closed\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **ci: strict_required_status_checks_policy on the main branch ruleset is false, so merged CI status can go stale relative to the base branch** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Workflow-quality review, 2026-08-18/19, adversarially reviewed and re-verified against live repo state 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n- **Note**: This item was filed via direct `gh issue create` rather than the `/dh:work-backlog-item create` skill \u2014 that skill's session-start bash injection (`!`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"`\\\\`` on SKILL.md line 9) fails with `permission denied: ../..` when invoked from an agent session whose cwd is a nested worktree (`.claude/worktrees/<name>/`), reproduced with zero args passed. A companion backlog item should be filed for that skill-loading defect itself.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b00b81dd681bda0b116a2d267d86b05d8700ca9c6108483b1b2f957e1b747243\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIgXw\"}"}